<article class="wiki-article"><p class="starter-reading-note" data-copy-en="Select a screenshot to enlarge it. Screens show example inventories and progress." data-copy-zh="点击截图可放大查看。图中的库存和进度仅为示例，请以自己的实际情况为准。">Select a screenshot to enlarge it. Screens show example inventories and progress.</p><div class="wiki-source-content wiki-source-content-en" data-lang-panel="en" lang="en"><section id="en-overview"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Quick_Start"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Blacksmith_Shop_(Kings_Demesne,_Medieval)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Blacksmith_Shop_.28Kings_Demesne.2C_Medieval.29"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Village_Market_(Village_Outskirts,_Medieval)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Village_Market_.28Village_Outskirts.2C_Medieval.29"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Mountain_Foothills_(Village_Outskirts,_Medieval)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Mountain_Foothills_.28Village_Outskirts.2C_Medieval.29"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Tutorial_quest"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="How_He_Works"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="His_Pricing"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Dragon_Coin_Planning"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="The_Four_Pieces"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="The_Four_Tiers"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Finding_the_four_required_drops"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="What_Each_Project_Unlocks"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Why_the_Order_Matters"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Troubleshooting"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="The_dungeon_blacksmith_is_unavailable"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Iron_Ore_&amp;_Mithril_Ore_Quests"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Iron_Ore_.26_Mithril_Ore_Quests"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Talking_to_Gastoff_(Stat_Rewards)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Talking_to_Gastoff_.28Stat_Rewards.29"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Talk_to_Gastoff"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Musclecraft_Exchange_(Body_Builder_only)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Musclecraft_Exchange_.28Body_Builder_only.29"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Admire_Armor"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Tips_and_Strategy"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Related_Pages"></span>
<h2>Three ways Gastoff helps you grow</h2>
<p>Gastoff’s Blacksmith Shop handles your ordinary melee weapon and armor, four additional Forge pieces, and a group of major construction commissions. These use separate resources and progress independently.</p>
<ul><li><strong>Starting equipment:</strong> spend Wealth and Supplies Materials to raise your sword and main armor through level 5.</li><li><strong>Forge pieces:</strong> spend mining resources to make Gauntlets, a Helmet, a Shield and Pauldrons. Their passive effects stack with your main equipment.</li><li><strong>Construction:</strong> commission new facilities once you meet their reputation, resource and other requirements.</li></ul>
<p>For a first visit, check which equipment slot is still level 0. A sword or armor purchase costs $150 and 20 minutes. For your first Forge piece, bring <strong>10 Iron Ingots and 1 Mineral Cluster</strong>; choose the benefit you need from the combat table below.</p>
</section>
<section id="en-start"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Locations"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Where_Ingots_Come_From"></span>
<h2>Where to go and what to bring</h2>
<p>Visit <strong>Medieval → Kings Demesne → Merchants Quarter → Blacksmith Shop</strong>, from <strong>06:00 to 21:00</strong>. Gastoff is there every day during those hours. His introduction plays automatically on your first eligible visit.</p>
<p>The <strong>Village Market</strong> in Village Outskirts offers the same level-1 sword and armor purchases, during the same hours. Return to Gastoff for the ordinary upgrades after that. A <strong>Martial Artist</strong> starts with melee level 1; a <strong>Body Builder or Athlete</strong> starts with armor level 1, so that slot skips its initial purchase.</p>
<p>Open <strong>Use the Forge</strong> at the shop to craft the extra pieces. Opening the screen and forging cost no Wealth or in-game time; crafting consumes the listed resources. Supplies Materials cannot substitute for mining ingots. Check whole resource counts: fragment progress is not spendable as a whole ingot.</p>
<figure class="reviewed-screenshot"><a aria-label="View full screenshot: Kings Demesne: enter Merchants Quarter to reach the Blacksmith Shop." href="../assets/images/wiki/forge/en-map.webp" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><img alt="Kings Demesne: enter Merchants Quarter to reach the Blacksmith Shop." decoding="async" height="720" loading="lazy" src="../assets/images/wiki/forge/en-map.webp" width="1280"/></a><figcaption>Kings Demesne: enter Merchants Quarter to reach the Blacksmith Shop.</figcaption></figure></section>
<section id="en-forge"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Gastoff's_Forge_—_The_Four_Armor_Pieces"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Gastoff.27s_Forge_.E2.80.94_The_Four_Armor_Pieces"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Forge_Costs"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Reading_the_Forge_Screen"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Forge_Armor_Benefits"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="The_Forge_button_is_disabled"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Forge_Philosophy_(one-time_stat_boost)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Forge_Philosophy_.28one-time_stat_boost.29"></span>
<h2>Five Forge tiers, four independent pieces</h2>
<p>Each piece advances in order: <strong>Iron → Silver → Mithril → Gemmed → Chronium</strong>. You cannot skip a tier. Crafting replaces that piece’s previous version. All four are passive Key Items: owning them applies their effects, with no equipment-slot assignment.</p>
<table><caption>Cost of one piece at each step</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">New tier</th><th scope="col">Resources consumed</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">Iron</th><td data-label="Resources consumed">10 Iron Ingots + 1 Mineral Cluster</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Silver</th><td data-label="Resources consumed">10 Silver Ingots + 2 Mineral Clusters</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Mithril</th><td data-label="Resources consumed">10 Mithril Ingots + 3 Mineral Clusters</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Gemmed</th><td data-label="Resources consumed">20 Silver Ingots + 20 Mithril Ingots + 10 Gems + 10 matching monster drops</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Chronium</th><td data-label="Resources consumed">10 Chronium; requires the Gemmed piece and Cid’s Chronium introduction</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>The screen shows your highest owned tier and the next available upgrade. An unaffordable button is disabled. The final label is <strong>Max tier</strong>. A Gemmed piece can display that label before you unlock Chronium; completing Cid’s introduction reveals the next step.</p>
<figure class="reviewed-screenshot"><a aria-label="View full screenshot: Each piece starts at Iron. Its button lists the resources consumed for that piece." href="../assets/images/wiki/forge/en-first-piece.webp" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><img alt="Each piece starts at Iron. Its button lists the resources consumed for that piece." decoding="async" height="720" loading="lazy" src="../assets/images/wiki/forge/en-first-piece.webp" width="1280"/></a><figcaption>Each piece starts at Iron. Its button lists the resources consumed for that piece.</figcaption></figure></section>
<section id="en-combat">
<h2>What each piece does in combat</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Piece or effect</th><th scope="col">Iron</th><th scope="col">Silver</th><th scope="col">Mithril / Gemmed / Chronium</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">Gauntlets</th><td data-label="Iron">Enemy skill minimum roll −1</td><td data-label="Silver">−2</td><td data-label="Mithril / Gemmed / Chronium">−3</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Helmet</th><td data-label="Iron">Critical-hit damage −10%</td><td data-label="Silver">−20%</td><td data-label="Mithril / Gemmed / Chronium">−30%</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Shield: automatic partial block</th><td data-label="Iron">6% chance; blocks 3–7%</td><td data-label="Silver">12% chance; blocks 6–14%</td><td data-label="Mithril / Gemmed / Chronium">18% chance; blocks 9–21%</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Shield: reaction test</th><td data-label="Iron">Target +10 px; time +0.1 s</td><td data-label="Silver">+20 px; +0.2 s</td><td data-label="Mithril / Gemmed / Chronium">+30 px; +0.3 s</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Pauldrons: original armor bonus</th><td data-label="Iron">+1 effective armor</td><td data-label="Silver">+2</td><td data-label="Mithril / Gemmed / Chronium">+3</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p><strong>Gemmed adds +1 effective armor per piece; Chronium adds +2 per piece.</strong> These bonuses are additional to the Pauldrons’ original effect. Gemmed Pauldrons therefore give +4 in total, and Chronium Pauldrons give +5. A complete Gemmed set gives <strong>+7 effective armor</strong>; a complete Chronium set gives <strong>+11</strong>.</p>
<p>The original special effects stop improving at Mithril. Gauntlets lower the bottom of the enemy skill’s base damage range, to a minimum of 1; they do not subtract a fixed amount from every hit. Helmets reduce damage from critical hits rather than their frequency. Shields have separate automatic-block and manual-reaction benefits; the reaction-time bonus is applied before combat difficulty adjusts timing. None of these changes your stored main armor level.</p>
</section>
<section id="en-materials"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Gemmed_Materials_and_Mining"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Resource_checklist"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Mining_supplies"></span>
<h2>Mining resources and Gemmed drops</h2>
<p>Mine at <strong>Medieval → Village Outskirts → Mountain Foothills</strong>. Every 100 fragments of an ordinary resource become one whole unit. Iron, Silver and Mithril Ingots and Mineral Clusters stay in mining inventory; whole Gems and Crystals join your resource totals. Clusters also have fragment progress.</p>
<table><caption>Gemmed recipes require ten of the indicated drop</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Piece</th><th scope="col">Drop</th><th scope="col">Example Infinity enemies</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">Gauntlets</th><td data-label="Drop">Void-Touched Fang ×10</td><td data-label="Example Infinity enemies">Hellhound, Werewolf, Wolf, Goblin</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Helmet</th><td data-label="Drop">Abyssal Eye ×10</td><td data-label="Example Infinity enemies">Angler Beast, Kraken, Medusa, Giant Octopus</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Shield</th><td data-label="Drop">Shimmering Heartscale ×10</td><td data-label="Example Infinity enemies">Naga, Lamia, Sea Serpent, Sharkman</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Pauldrons</th><td data-label="Drop">Gilded Heart ×10</td><td data-label="Example Infinity enemies">Goldman, Succubus, Phoenix</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>These are eligible sources, not guaranteed rewards. Ordinary Infinity loot starts at <strong>1% on floors 1–5</strong>, rises by one percentage point every five floors, and caps at <strong>20% on floor 96+</strong>. Boss multipliers, affixes, Thieves Gloves and individual encounter rules can change the chance. An enemy with several eligible rewards does not always select the drop you want.</p>
<p>Infinity also redirects overstocked loot: a selected collectible above 125% of the average stock across the six monster-drop types, Gems and Leather may become one of your three least-stocked types. Check the actual victory reward. Marked bosses can also make a separate special-drop roll.</p>
<details><summary>Budget for all four pieces</summary><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Complete set through</th><th scope="col">Total from no Forge pieces</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">Mithril</th><td data-label="Total from no Forge pieces">40 Iron + 40 Silver + 40 Mithril Ingots; 24 Mineral Clusters</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Gemmed</th><td data-label="Total from no Forge pieces">40 Iron + 120 Silver + 120 Mithril Ingots; 24 Clusters; 40 Gems; 10 of each required drop</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Chronium</th><td data-label="Total from no Forge pieces">The full Gemmed total, plus 40 Chronium</td></tr>
</tbody></table></details>
<figure class="reviewed-screenshot"><a aria-label="View full screenshot: With Mithril pieces owned, the next recipes require Gems and a different monster drop for each piece." href="../assets/images/wiki/forge/en-gemmed.webp" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><img alt="With Mithril pieces owned, the next recipes require Gems and a different monster drop for each piece." decoding="async" height="720" loading="lazy" src="../assets/images/wiki/forge/en-gemmed.webp" width="1280"/></a><figcaption>With Mithril pieces owned, the next recipes require Gems and a different monster drop for each piece.</figcaption></figure></section>
<section id="en-chronium">
<h2>Unlocking Chronium</h2>
<p>After main story beat 65, speak to <strong>Cid at the Modification Clinic</strong> and complete <strong>Something That Holds</strong>. This gifts one Chronium and unlocks its collection and uses. Each successful source below awards one whole piece; Chronium does not use fragment conversion.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Source</th><th scope="col">Condition and chance after the introduction</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">Dwarf Miner</th><td data-label="Condition and chance after the introduction">Familiarity 10+; third choice; independent 8% bonus</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Unlimited Fortress Defense</th><td data-label="Condition and chance after the introduction">30+ completed waves; independent 25% chance on a qualifying return</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Infinity bosses</th><td data-label="Condition and chance after the introduction">Independent 5% from the specific bosses listed below; ordinary loot modifiers do not affect it</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Mining</th><td data-label="Condition and chance after the introduction">0.01% per eligible tile check; ore has 400 HP and must be broken; at most one deposit spawns per visit</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Present Hike Mountains</th><td data-label="Condition and chance after the introduction">0.5%; replaces the caterpillar find</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Medieval Back Alleys search</th><td data-label="Condition and chance after the introduction">0.5% after priority quest outcomes; replaces the ordinary encounter</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<details><summary>Eligible Infinity bosses</summary><p>Vampire Lord, Skeleton King, Emerald Dragon, Balrog, Phantom Captain, Cthulhu, Dark Sylph, Grim Reaper, ARIA Proxy Warden and Mech Siege Tank.</p></details>
<p>Chronium’s other uses compete for the same mineral. In particular, Anthrax’s one-time <strong>Strengthen Weapon</strong> action costs 10 Chronium for <strong>+1 effective melee weapon level</strong>; it leaves the weapon’s stored base level unchanged.</p>
<figure class="reviewed-screenshot"><a aria-label="View full screenshot: After Cid’s introduction, each Gemmed piece can become Chronium for 10 whole Chronium." href="../assets/images/wiki/forge/en-chronium.webp" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><img alt="After Cid’s introduction, each Gemmed piece can become Chronium for 10 whole Chronium." decoding="async" height="720" loading="lazy" src="../assets/images/wiki/forge/en-chronium.webp" width="1280"/></a><figcaption>After Cid’s introduction, each Gemmed piece can become Chronium for 10 whole Chronium.</figcaption></figure><figure class="reviewed-screenshot"><a aria-label="View full screenshot: A completed set: all four pieces show Chronium as their current tier." href="../assets/images/wiki/forge/en-complete.webp" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><img alt="A completed set: all four pieces show Chronium as their current tier." decoding="async" height="720" loading="lazy" src="../assets/images/wiki/forge/en-complete.webp" width="1280"/></a><figcaption>A completed set: all four pieces show Chronium as their current tier.</figcaption></figure></section>
<section id="en-equipment-reference"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Buying_Your_First_Sword_and_Armor"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Upgrading_Your_Sword_and_Armor_at_Gastoff"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Current_equipment_labels"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="A_sword_or_armor_upgrade_is_missing"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Other_Ways_to_Upgrade_Gear"></span>
<h2>Sword and main armor reference</h2>
<p>Gastoff offers the purchase at stored level 0 and only the next ordinary upgrade at levels 1–4. The following costs apply separately to sword and armor, before modifiers.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Step</th><th scope="col">Wealth</th><th scope="col">Supplies Materials</th><th scope="col">Time</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">0 → 1</th><td data-label="Wealth">$150</td><td data-label="Supplies Materials">None</td><td data-label="Time">20 min</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">1 → 2</th><td data-label="Wealth">$250</td><td data-label="Supplies Materials">30 common</td><td data-label="Time">20 min</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">2 → 3</th><td data-label="Wealth">$600</td><td data-label="Supplies Materials">20 rare</td><td data-label="Time">20 min</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">3 → 4</th><td data-label="Wealth">$1,200</td><td data-label="Supplies Materials">10 epic</td><td data-label="Time">45 min</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">4 → 5</th><td data-label="Wealth">$10,000</td><td data-label="Supplies Materials">40 common + 25 rare + 15 epic</td><td data-label="Time">20 min</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>One slot from 0 to 5 totals <strong>$12,200, 70 common + 45 rare + 25 epic Materials, and 125 minutes</strong>. The tutorial quest <strong>Forged in Fire</strong> awards +2 Strength when your melee weapon reaches level 3 or higher; armor does not satisfy it.</p>
<details><summary>Equipment names at every stored level</summary><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Level</th><th scope="col">Melee weapon</th><th scope="col">Main armor</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">0</th><td data-label="Melee weapon">Wooden Club</td><td data-label="Main armor">Tattered Rags</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">1</th><td data-label="Melee weapon">Wooden Sword</td><td data-label="Main armor">Leather Armor</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">2</th><td data-label="Melee weapon">Bronze Sword</td><td data-label="Main armor">Chainmail Armor</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">3</th><td data-label="Melee weapon">Iron Sword</td><td data-label="Main armor">Plated Armor</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">4</th><td data-label="Melee weapon">Steel Sword</td><td data-label="Main armor">Knight Armor</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">5</th><td data-label="Melee weapon">Mithril Sword</td><td data-label="Main armor">Royal Armor</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">6</th><td data-label="Melee weapon">Enchanted Sword</td><td data-label="Main armor">Bone Armor</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">7</th><td data-label="Melee weapon">Infernal Sword</td><td data-label="Main armor">Infernal Armor</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">8</th><td data-label="Melee weapon">Runic Sword</td><td data-label="Main armor">Divine Armor</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">9</th><td data-label="Melee weapon">Divine Sword</td><td data-label="Main armor">Prismatic Armor</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">10</th><td data-label="Melee weapon">Celestial Sword</td><td data-label="Main armor">Celestial Armor</td></tr>
</tbody></table></details>
</section>
<section id="en-minotaur"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Minotaur_Blacksmith_(Dungeon_Floor_26)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Minotaur_Blacksmith_.28Dungeon_Floor_26.29"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="The_Minotaur_Blacksmith_(Dungeon)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="The_Minotaur_Blacksmith_.28Dungeon.29"></span>
<h2>The Minotaur Blacksmith on floor 26</h2>
<p>Normal dungeon floor 26 contains his fixed chamber, surrounded by a lava ring. Step onto his tile to interact. He accepts <strong>Dragon Coins</strong> and upgrades a stored melee weapon or armor level <strong>1–7 by one</strong>, reaching level 8. Level 0 and level 8+ equipment are ineligible.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Upgrade</th><th scope="col">Dragon Coins</th><th scope="col">Upgrade</th><th scope="col">Dragon Coins</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">1 → 2</th><td data-label="Dragon Coins">3</td><td data-label="Upgrade">5 → 6</td><td data-label="Dragon Coins">7</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">2 → 3</th><td data-label="Dragon Coins">4</td><td data-label="Upgrade">6 → 7</td><td data-label="Dragon Coins">8</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">3 → 4</th><td data-label="Dragon Coins">5</td><td data-label="Upgrade">7 → 8</td><td data-label="Dragon Coins">9</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">4 → 5</th><td data-label="Dragon Coins">6</td><td data-label="Upgrade"></td><td data-label="Dragon Coins"></td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>One interaction buys one upgrade. <strong>His tile remains: move away and return for another interaction.</strong> Leaving the dungeon is unnecessary. Budget 42 Coins for one slot from 1 to 8, or 24 from Gastoff’s level 5 to 8; both slots cost twice as much. Reaching his chamber does not supply the required Coins.</p>
<p>For further progression, <strong>Sylwithe’s Hollow</strong> offers repeatable +1 stored melee, armor or ranged levels for <strong>10 Crystals each, up to level 10</strong>. Aziza’s ordinary Grimoire upgrade is a separate level-1-to-2 purchase for $1,000 and 30 minutes; ranged weapons have their own upgrade routes.</p>
</section>
<section id="en-construction"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Brothel_Construction_Commissions"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Construction_Costs_and_Prerequisites"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Construction_and_Training_Details"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="A_construction_action_is_missing"></span>
<h2>Gastoff’s construction commissions</h2>
<p>Commission these through Gastoff’s character actions at the shop. The facilities open when their construction scene finishes; there is no multi-day building queue. Resource quantities below are required <strong>in each of Materials, Ingredients and Fabrics</strong>. Costs are before modifiers.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Project</th><th scope="col">Wealth</th><th scope="col">Each crafting resource</th><th scope="col">Rep</th><th scope="col">Other prerequisite</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">Courtyard</th><td data-label="Wealth">$30,000</td><td data-label="Each crafting resource">10 epic</td><td data-label="Rep">5</td><td data-label="Other prerequisite">—</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Pool</th><td data-label="Wealth">$200,000</td><td data-label="Each crafting resource">25 epic</td><td data-label="Rep">6</td><td data-label="Other prerequisite">Courtyard</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Menagerie</th><td data-label="Wealth">$2,000,000</td><td data-label="Each crafting resource">50 epic</td><td data-label="Rep">9</td><td data-label="Other prerequisite">Courtyard</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Training Room</th><td data-label="Wealth">$10,000,000</td><td data-label="Each crafting resource">500 common + 200 rare + 75 epic</td><td data-label="Rep">9</td><td data-label="Other prerequisite">—</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Cell Corridor + Cell 1</th><td data-label="Wealth">$1,000,000</td><td data-label="Each crafting resource">35 rare</td><td data-label="Rep">8</td><td data-label="Other prerequisite">Raven active; paid content access</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Cell 2</th><td data-label="Wealth">$1,500,000</td><td data-label="Each crafting resource">50 rare</td><td data-label="Rep">—</td><td data-label="Other prerequisite">Corridor; paid content access</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Cell 3</th><td data-label="Wealth">$2,000,000</td><td data-label="Each crafting resource">25 epic</td><td data-label="Rep">—</td><td data-label="Other prerequisite">Cell 2; paid content access</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Cell 4</th><td data-label="Wealth">$2,500,000</td><td data-label="Each crafting resource">30 epic</td><td data-label="Rep">—</td><td data-label="Other prerequisite">Cell 3; paid content access</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Cell 5</th><td data-label="Wealth">$3,000,000</td><td data-label="Each crafting resource">35 epic</td><td data-label="Rep">—</td><td data-label="Other prerequisite">Cell 4; paid content access</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Cell 6</th><td data-label="Wealth">$3,500,000</td><td data-label="Each crafting resource">40 epic</td><td data-label="Rep">—</td><td data-label="Other prerequisite">Cell 5; paid content access</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Cell 7</th><td data-label="Wealth">$4,000,000</td><td data-label="Each crafting resource">45 epic</td><td data-label="Rep">—</td><td data-label="Other prerequisite">Cell 6; paid content access</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>Most commissions take <strong>3 hours</strong>; the Menagerie takes <strong>3 hours 20 minutes</strong>, and the Training Room <strong>4 hours</strong>. The complete corridor-and-seven-cell chain costs <strong>$17,500,000</strong>. Cell 8 is unavailable.</p>
<p>The Courtyard connects outdoor facilities; the Pool is required for Sashimi’s move to the house; the warded Menagerie houses magical creatures. Courtyard, Pool, Menagerie and Training Room each add one decor level. The corridor includes Cell 1 and opens the holding-cell area; additional cells expand capacity sequentially.</p>
</section>
<section id="en-training"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Training_Room_apprentices"></span>
<h2>Using the Training Room</h2>
<p>Train Strength, Stamina, Ability or Mystic. A session has base costs of <strong>$80,000, 50 Energy and 50 Calm</strong>, with no ordinary daily use cap. Assigned apprentices improve the time and weighted stat gain.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Apprentices</th><th scope="col">Time</th><th scope="col">Possible gain</th><th scope="col">Weights, lowest to highest</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">0</th><td data-label="Time">120 min</td><td data-label="Possible gain">+2 to +5</td><td data-label="Weights, lowest to highest">25%, 40%, 25%, 10%</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">1</th><td data-label="Time">120 min</td><td data-label="Possible gain">+2 to +6</td><td data-label="Weights, lowest to highest">10%, 25%, 35%, 20%, 10%</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">2</th><td data-label="Time">100 min</td><td data-label="Possible gain">+2 to +6</td><td data-label="Weights, lowest to highest">10%, 25%, 35%, 20%, 10%</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">3</th><td data-label="Time">100 min</td><td data-label="Possible gain">+3 to +7</td><td data-label="Weights, lowest to highest">10%, 25%, 35%, 20%, 10%</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>These are player-stat sessions, separate from worker training. Other applicable action modifiers may further adjust the displayed costs.</p>
</section>
<section id="en-rewards">
<h2>Conversations, rewards and ore requests</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Action</th><th scope="col">Requirements</th><th scope="col">Time and result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Talk to Gastoff</th><td data-label="Requirements">Up to 6 talks per day</td><td data-label="Time and result">10 min; +1 base relationship before modifiers</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Forge Philosophy</th><td data-label="Requirements">Known or higher; Communication 48+</td><td data-label="Time and result">30 min; one-time +1 Strength, +10 relationship</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Musclecraft Exchange</th><td data-label="Requirements">Acknowledged or higher; Body Builder</td><td data-label="Time and result">40 min; one-time +1 Attractiveness, +5 relationship</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Admire Armor</th><td data-label="Requirements">Shop hours</td><td data-label="Time and result">5 min; +1 Calm</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>Construction also raises Gastoff’s relationship: Courtyard +10; Pool +15; Menagerie +15 and Aziza +15; Training Room +20; Corridor and each extra cell +10.</p>
<p>The Fighters Guild’s <strong>Iron Ore Sample</strong> quest needs five samples from floors 6–10 and pays $150, 2 Clout and 1 Crystal. <strong>Mithril Ore Sample</strong> needs five from floors 16–20 and pays $250, 3 Clout and 1 Crystal. Accept and turn them in at the guild. While the relevant quest is active, each eligible generated floor has a 50% ore-spawn check. Collecting the tile does not start a separate fight, and quest ore is separate from mining ingots.</p>
</section>
<section id="en-troubleshooting">
<h2>If an option is missing</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Sword or armor:</strong> check the exact stored level and shop hours. Gastoff’s normal ladder ends at 5.</li><li><strong>Forge:</strong> check the preceding piece tier and whole resource quantities. For Chronium, finish Cid’s introduction and own the Gemmed piece.</li><li><strong>Minotaur:</strong> bring enough Dragon Coins for the selected level; move off his persistent tile and return to interact again.</li><li><strong>Construction:</strong> check reputation, the preceding project, paid content access where required, and Raven’s active status for the corridor. Completed projects disappear from the commission list.</li></ul>
</section>
<section id="en-related"><h2>Related guides</h2><p>Use <a href="game-systems-mining-system.html">Mining</a> to plan resource gathering, <a href="game-systems-combat-system.html">Combat System</a> for damage calculations, and <a href="game-systems-infinity-dungeons.html">Infinity Dungeons</a> for enemy loot. For the next equipment levels, see <a href="game-systems-sylwithes-hollow.html">Sylwithe’s Hollow</a>; for facility management, see <a href="game-systems-brothel.html">Brothel</a>.</p></section>
</div><div class="wiki-source-content wiki-source-content-zh" data-lang-panel="zh" hidden="" lang="zh-CN"><section id="zh-overview"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Quick_Start"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Blacksmith_Shop_(Kings_Demesne,_Medieval)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Blacksmith_Shop_.28Kings_Demesne.2C_Medieval.29"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Village_Market_(Village_Outskirts,_Medieval)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Village_Market_.28Village_Outskirts.2C_Medieval.29"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Mountain_Foothills_(Village_Outskirts,_Medieval)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Mountain_Foothills_.28Village_Outskirts.2C_Medieval.29"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Tutorial_quest"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-How_He_Works"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-His_Pricing"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Dragon_Coin_Planning"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-The_Four_Pieces"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-The_Four_Tiers"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Finding_the_four_required_drops"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-What_Each_Project_Unlocks"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Why_the_Order_Matters"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Troubleshooting"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-The_dungeon_blacksmith_is_unavailable"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Iron_Ore_&amp;_Mithril_Ore_Quests"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Iron_Ore_.26_Mithril_Ore_Quests"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Talking_to_Gastoff_(Stat_Rewards)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Talking_to_Gastoff_.28Stat_Rewards.29"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Talk_to_Gastoff"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Musclecraft_Exchange_(Body_Builder_only)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Musclecraft_Exchange_.28Body_Builder_only.29"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Admire_Armor"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Tips_and_Strategy"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Related_Pages"></span>
<h2>先分清三条成长路线</h2>
<p>Gastoff 的铁匠铺既能升级近战武器和主护甲，也能锻造四种额外护具，还承接多项大型扩建。这三套系统分别消耗不同资源，进度互不替代。</p>
<ul><li><strong>基础装备：</strong>花费财富和补给栏中的材料，将剑与主护甲逐步升到 5 级。</li><li><strong>锻造护具：</strong>用采矿资源打造护手、头盔、盾牌和肩甲。它们提供被动效果，可与主装备叠加。</li><li><strong>建筑委托：</strong>满足声誉、资源和其他条件后，委托 Gastoff 建造新设施。</li></ul>
<p>第一次来，先看看哪个装备栏位仍是 0 级。购买剑或护甲各需 <strong>$150 和 20 分钟</strong>。想打造第一件额外护具，则准备 <strong>10 铁锭和 1 矿物簇</strong>，再根据下方的战斗效果表选择部位。</p>
</section>
<section id="zh-start"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Locations"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Where_Ingots_Come_From"></span>
<h2>地点、营业时间与准备</h2>
<p>路线为<strong>中世纪 → 国王领地 → 商人区 → 铁匠铺</strong>，营业时间是每天 <strong>06:00–21:00</strong>。Gastoff 在这段时间都在店里；首次符合条件地到访时，会自动播放他的介绍剧情。</p>
<p>村庄郊外的<strong>村庄市场</strong>也在同一时段出售相同的 1 级剑和护甲。之后的常规升级要回铁匠铺完成。<strong>武术家</strong>开局已有 1 级近战武器；<strong>健美者和运动员</strong>开局已有 1 级护甲，因此不必重复购买对应装备。</p>
<p>在店里选择<strong>「使用熔炉」</strong>即可打开锻造界面。打开界面与打造护具都不消耗财富或游戏时间，只扣除配方列出的资源。补给栏中的普通、稀有、史诗材料不能代替矿锭。出发前确认已有足够的<strong>整单位资源</strong>；尚未凑满的碎片不能按一整锭使用。</p>
<figure class="reviewed-screenshot"><a aria-label="查看完整截图：国王领地：进入商人区，即可找到铁匠铺。" href="../assets/images/wiki/forge/zh-map.webp" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><img alt="国王领地：进入商人区，即可找到铁匠铺。" decoding="async" height="720" loading="lazy" src="../assets/images/wiki/forge/zh-map.webp" width="1280"/></a><figcaption>国王领地：进入商人区，即可找到铁匠铺。</figcaption></figure></section>
<section id="zh-forge"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Gastoff's_Forge_—_The_Four_Armor_Pieces"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Gastoff.27s_Forge_.E2.80.94_The_Four_Armor_Pieces"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Forge_Costs"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Reading_the_Forge_Screen"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Forge_Armor_Benefits"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-The_Forge_button_is_disabled"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Forge_Philosophy_(one-time_stat_boost)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Forge_Philosophy_.28one-time_stat_boost.29"></span>
<h2>四个部位，五个等级</h2>
<p>每个部位都按<strong>铁 → 银 → 秘银 → 宝石镶嵌 → 时源矿</strong>的顺序升级，不能跳级。打造下一等级会替换同部位的旧护具。四件护具都是被动生效的关键物品，持有即可，无须分配装备栏位。</p>
<table><caption>每个部位每次升级的消耗</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">目标等级</th><th scope="col">所需资源</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">铁</th><td data-label="所需资源">10 铁锭 + 1 矿物簇</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">银</th><td data-label="所需资源">10 银锭 + 2 矿物簇</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">秘银</th><td data-label="所需资源">10 秘银锭 + 3 矿物簇</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">宝石镶嵌</th><td data-label="所需资源">20 银锭 + 20 秘银锭 + 10 宝石 + 10 个对应怪物掉落物</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">时源矿</th><td data-label="所需资源">10 时源矿；须持有该部位的宝石护具，并完成 Cid 的时源矿介绍剧情</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>界面会显示当前最高等级与下一项可用升级。资源不足时，按钮无法点击。达到当前可用的最高等级时会显示满级提示；如果尚未完成 Cid 的介绍，宝石护具也可能暂时显示这个提示，完成介绍后才会出现时源矿升级。</p>
<figure class="reviewed-screenshot"><a aria-label="查看完整截图：四个部位都从铁级开始。每个按钮分别列出该部位的打造费用。" href="../assets/images/wiki/forge/zh-first-piece.webp" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><img alt="四个部位都从铁级开始。每个按钮分别列出该部位的打造费用。" decoding="async" height="720" loading="lazy" src="../assets/images/wiki/forge/zh-first-piece.webp" width="1280"/></a><figcaption>四个部位都从铁级开始。每个按钮分别列出该部位的打造费用。</figcaption></figure></section>
<section id="zh-combat">
<h2>护具的战斗效果</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th scope="col">部位或效果</th><th scope="col">铁</th><th scope="col">银</th><th scope="col">秘银／宝石／时源矿</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">护手</th><td data-label="铁">敌人技能伤害掷值下限 −1</td><td data-label="银">−2</td><td data-label="秘银／宝石／时源矿">−3</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">头盔</th><td data-label="铁">受到的暴击伤害 −10%</td><td data-label="银">−20%</td><td data-label="秘银／宝石／时源矿">−30%</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">盾牌：自动部分格挡</th><td data-label="铁">6% 概率；减伤 3–7%</td><td data-label="银">12% 概率；减伤 6–14%</td><td data-label="秘银／宝石／时源矿">18% 概率；减伤 9–21%</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">盾牌：反应判定</th><td data-label="铁">目标增大 10 像素；时间 +0.1 秒</td><td data-label="银">+20 像素；+0.2 秒</td><td data-label="秘银／宝石／时源矿">+30 像素；+0.3 秒</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">肩甲：原有护甲加成</th><td data-label="铁">有效护甲等级 +1</td><td data-label="银">+2</td><td data-label="秘银／宝石／时源矿">+3</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p><strong>每件宝石护具另加 1 级有效护甲，每件时源矿护具另加 2 级。</strong>这部分会与肩甲原有的加成相加。因此，宝石肩甲合计加 4 级，时源矿肩甲合计加 5 级；四件宝石护具共加 <strong>7 级有效护甲</strong>，四件时源矿护具共加 <strong>11 级</strong>。</p>
<p>各部位原有的特殊效果在秘银阶段达到上限。护手降低的是敌人技能基础伤害范围的下限，最低降到 1，并非每次受击都固定减去同样伤害。头盔降低暴击造成的伤害，不降低暴击概率。盾牌的自动格挡与手动反应判定分别生效；反应时间加成会先加入，再按战斗难度调整。上述加成都不会改变主护甲栏位显示的基础等级。</p>
</section>
<section id="zh-materials"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Gemmed_Materials_and_Mining"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Resource_checklist"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Mining_supplies"></span>
<h2>采矿资源与宝石护具材料</h2>
<p>采矿地点是<strong>中世纪 → 村庄郊外 → 山脚</strong>。普通矿物资源每攒满 100 碎片会合成 1 个整单位。铁锭、银锭、秘银锭和矿物簇留在采矿库存；完整的宝石与水晶计入角色资源。矿物簇同样需要积累碎片，发现一块相关矿石不等于直接获得一个完整矿物簇。</p>
<table><caption>每件宝石护具需要 10 个对应掉落物</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">部位</th><th scope="col">掉落物</th><th scope="col">无限地下城中的来源示例</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">护手</th><td data-label="掉落物">虚触之牙 ×10</td><td data-label="无限地下城中的来源示例">地狱犬、狼人、狼、哥布林</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">头盔</th><td data-label="掉落物">深渊之眼 ×10</td><td data-label="无限地下城中的来源示例">鮟鱇兽、克拉肯、美杜莎、巨型章鱼</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">盾牌</th><td data-label="掉落物">微光心鳞 ×10</td><td data-label="无限地下城中的来源示例">娜迦、拉弥亚、海蛇、鲨鱼人</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">肩甲</th><td data-label="掉落物">鎏金之心 ×10</td><td data-label="无限地下城中的来源示例">Goldman、魅魔、凤凰</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>表中是可能的来源，并不保证击杀后掉落。无限地下城的普通掉落基础概率在 <strong>1–5 层为 1%</strong>，之后每 5 层提高 1 个百分点，到 <strong>96 层起封顶 20%</strong>。首领倍率、词缀、盗贼手套和特定遭遇规则还会调整概率。某个敌人有多种候选掉落时，也不一定选中你需要的材料。</p>
<p>无限地下城还会平衡库存：六类怪物掉落物、宝石和皮革中，若本次选中物品的存量高于这八类物品平均存量的 125%，它可能改为库存最少的三类之一。应以胜利结算实际显示的奖励为准。带有相应标记的首领另有一次特殊掉落判定。</p>
<details><summary>四件护具的总资源预算</summary><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">整套达到</th><th scope="col">从零开始的累计消耗</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">秘银</th><td data-label="从零开始的累计消耗">40 铁锭 + 40 银锭 + 40 秘银锭；24 矿物簇</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">宝石镶嵌</th><td data-label="从零开始的累计消耗">40 铁锭 + 120 银锭 + 120 秘银锭；24 矿物簇；40 宝石；四种指定掉落物各 10 个</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">时源矿</th><td data-label="从零开始的累计消耗">整套宝石护具的全部消耗，再加 40 时源矿</td></tr>
</tbody></table></details>
<figure class="reviewed-screenshot"><a aria-label="查看完整截图：持有秘银护具后，下一步需要宝石，以及各部位对应的怪物掉落物。" href="../assets/images/wiki/forge/zh-gemmed.webp" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><img alt="持有秘银护具后，下一步需要宝石，以及各部位对应的怪物掉落物。" decoding="async" height="720" loading="lazy" src="../assets/images/wiki/forge/zh-gemmed.webp" width="1280"/></a><figcaption>持有秘银护具后，下一步需要宝石，以及各部位对应的怪物掉落物。</figcaption></figure></section>
<section id="zh-chronium">
<h2>解锁时源矿</h2>
<p>完成主线第 65 段后，到<strong>改造诊所找 Cid</strong>，完成<strong>「坚守之物」</strong>。剧情会赠送 1 时源矿，并解锁它的收集与用途。下表各途径成功时都获得 1 个完整时源矿，不经过碎片合成。</p>
<table><thead><tr><th scope="col">途径</th><th scope="col">完成介绍剧情后的条件与概率</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">矮人矿工</th><td data-label="完成介绍剧情后的条件与概率">熟悉度 10 以上，选择第三项；独立 8% 额外奖励</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">无限要塞防御</th><td data-label="完成介绍剧情后的条件与概率">完成至少 30 波；符合条件地返回结算时独立判定 25%</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">无限地下城首领</th><td data-label="完成介绍剧情后的条件与概率">下列指定首领各有独立 5% 概率，不受普通战利品加成影响</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">采矿</th><td data-label="完成介绍剧情后的条件与概率">每次符合条件的矿块判定有 0.01% 概率；矿石有 400 生命，击碎才给奖励；每次采矿最多生成一处</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">现代的山间徒步</th><td data-label="完成介绍剧情后的条件与概率">0.5%；替换原本发现毛毛虫的结果</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">中世纪后巷搜索</th><td data-label="完成介绍剧情后的条件与概率">优先任务结果处理完后有 0.5%；替换普通遭遇</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<details><summary>哪些无限地下城首领能掉时源矿？</summary><p>吸血鬼领主、骷髅王、翡翠巨龙、Balrog、幽灵船长、Cthulhu、黑暗西尔芙、死神（Grim Reaper）、A.R.I.A.代理典狱官和机械攻城坦克。</p></details>
<p>时源矿的其他用途会与护具争夺同一份库存。例如，Anthrax 的一次性<strong>「强化武器」</strong>需要 10 时源矿，提供 <strong>1 级有效近战武器等级</strong>，但不会改变武器栏位的基础等级。</p>
<figure class="reviewed-screenshot"><a aria-label="查看完整截图：完成 Cid 的介绍剧情后，每件宝石护具可用 10 个完整时源矿升级。" href="../assets/images/wiki/forge/zh-chronium.webp" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><img alt="完成 Cid 的介绍剧情后，每件宝石护具可用 10 个完整时源矿升级。" decoding="async" height="720" loading="lazy" src="../assets/images/wiki/forge/zh-chronium.webp" width="1280"/></a><figcaption>完成 Cid 的介绍剧情后，每件宝石护具可用 10 个完整时源矿升级。</figcaption></figure><figure class="reviewed-screenshot"><a aria-label="查看完整截图：整套完成后的界面：四个部位的当前等级均为时源矿。" href="../assets/images/wiki/forge/zh-complete.webp" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><img alt="整套完成后的界面：四个部位的当前等级均为时源矿。" decoding="async" height="720" loading="lazy" src="../assets/images/wiki/forge/zh-complete.webp" width="1280"/></a><figcaption>整套完成后的界面：四个部位的当前等级均为时源矿。</figcaption></figure></section>
<section id="zh-equipment-reference"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Buying_Your_First_Sword_and_Armor"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Upgrading_Your_Sword_and_Armor_at_Gastoff"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Current_equipment_labels"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-A_sword_or_armor_upgrade_is_missing"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Other_Ways_to_Upgrade_Gear"></span>
<h2>剑与主护甲升级表</h2>
<p>装备基础等级恰好为 0 时，Gastoff 提供初次购买；为 1–4 级时，只显示对应的下一次常规升级。下表费用<strong>对剑和护甲分别收取</strong>，尚未计算通用行动修正。</p>
<table><thead><tr><th scope="col">升级</th><th scope="col">财富</th><th scope="col">补给栏材料</th><th scope="col">时间</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">0 → 1</th><td data-label="财富">$150</td><td data-label="补给栏材料">无</td><td data-label="时间">20 分钟</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">1 → 2</th><td data-label="财富">$250</td><td data-label="补给栏材料">30 普通</td><td data-label="时间">20 分钟</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">2 → 3</th><td data-label="财富">$600</td><td data-label="补给栏材料">20 稀有</td><td data-label="时间">20 分钟</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">3 → 4</th><td data-label="财富">$1,200</td><td data-label="补给栏材料">10 史诗</td><td data-label="时间">45 分钟</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">4 → 5</th><td data-label="财富">$10,000</td><td data-label="补给栏材料">40 普通 + 25 稀有 + 15 史诗</td><td data-label="时间">20 分钟</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>单个栏位从 0 升至 5 级，共需 <strong>$12,200、70 普通 + 45 稀有 + 25 史诗材料，以及 125 分钟</strong>。教程任务 <strong>「烈火锻造」</strong> 在近战武器达到 3 级以上时奖励 2 力量；只升级护甲无法完成这个目标。</p>
<details><summary>各基础等级的装备名称</summary><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">等级</th><th scope="col">近战武器</th><th scope="col">主护甲</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">0</th><td data-label="近战武器">木棒</td><td data-label="主护甲">破烂布衣</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">1</th><td data-label="近战武器">木剑</td><td data-label="主护甲">皮甲</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">2</th><td data-label="近战武器">青铜剑</td><td data-label="主护甲">锁子甲</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">3</th><td data-label="近战武器">铁剑</td><td data-label="主护甲">板甲</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">4</th><td data-label="近战武器">钢剑</td><td data-label="主护甲">骑士护甲</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">5</th><td data-label="近战武器">秘银剑</td><td data-label="主护甲">皇家护甲</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">6</th><td data-label="近战武器">附魔剑</td><td data-label="主护甲">骨甲</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">7</th><td data-label="近战武器">炼狱之剑</td><td data-label="主护甲">炼狱护甲</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">8</th><td data-label="近战武器">符文剑</td><td data-label="主护甲">神圣护甲</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">9</th><td data-label="近战武器">神圣之剑</td><td data-label="主护甲">棱彩护甲</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">10</th><td data-label="近战武器">天界之剑</td><td data-label="主护甲">天界护甲</td></tr>
</tbody></table></details>
</section>
<section id="zh-minotaur"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Minotaur_Blacksmith_(Dungeon_Floor_26)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Minotaur_Blacksmith_.28Dungeon_Floor_26.29"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-The_Minotaur_Blacksmith_(Dungeon)"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-The_Minotaur_Blacksmith_.28Dungeon.29"></span>
<h2>第 26 层的牛头人铁匠</h2>
<p>普通地下城第 26 层有一间固定锻造室，周围是一圈熔岩。走到牛头人铁匠的格子上即可互动。他只收<strong>龙币</strong>，能把基础等级为 <strong>1–7 级</strong>的近战武器或护甲提高 1 级，最高升至 8 级。0 级和 8 级以上的装备不符合条件。</p>
<table><thead><tr><th scope="col">升级</th><th scope="col">龙币</th><th scope="col">升级</th><th scope="col">龙币</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">1 → 2</th><td data-label="龙币">3</td><td data-label="升级">5 → 6</td><td data-label="龙币">7</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">2 → 3</th><td data-label="龙币">4</td><td data-label="升级">6 → 7</td><td data-label="龙币">8</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">3 → 4</th><td data-label="龙币">5</td><td data-label="升级">7 → 8</td><td data-label="龙币">9</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">4 → 5</th><td data-label="龙币">6</td><td data-label="升级"></td><td data-label="龙币"></td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>一次互动只能升级一次，但<strong>他的格子不会消失，离开该格再走回来就能重新互动</strong>，不必退出整个地下城。单件装备从 1 升到 8 级共需 42 龙币；从 Gastoff 的 5 级继续升至 8 级需 24 龙币。剑与护甲都升级则费用翻倍。抵达锻造室并不代表会自动获得所需龙币。</p>
<p>还想继续升级时，<strong>Sylwithe 的幽谷</strong>提供可重复购买的近战武器、护甲和远程武器升级，每次 <strong>10 水晶提高 1 级基础等级，最高 10 级</strong>。Aziza 的常规魔导书升级是另一项购买：$1,000、30 分钟，从 1 级升至 2 级；远程武器也有独立的成长途径。</p>
</section>
<section id="zh-construction"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Brothel_Construction_Commissions"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Construction_Costs_and_Prerequisites"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Construction_and_Training_Details"></span><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-A_construction_action_is_missing"></span>
<h2>Gastoff 的建筑委托</h2>
<p>在铁匠铺通过 Gastoff 的角色行动委托施工。建筑剧情结束后即可使用新设施，不需要等待多天。下表的资源数目是<strong>材料、食材、布料各需的数量</strong>；财富和时间均为修正前的基础费用。</p>
<table><thead><tr><th scope="col">项目</th><th scope="col">财富</th><th scope="col">每类制作资源</th><th scope="col">声誉</th><th scope="col">其他条件</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">庭院</th><td data-label="财富">$30,000</td><td data-label="每类制作资源">10 史诗</td><td data-label="声誉">5</td><td data-label="其他条件">—</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">水池</th><td data-label="财富">$200,000</td><td data-label="每类制作资源">25 史诗</td><td data-label="声誉">6</td><td data-label="其他条件">已建庭院</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">珍兽苑</th><td data-label="财富">$2,000,000</td><td data-label="每类制作资源">50 史诗</td><td data-label="声誉">9</td><td data-label="其他条件">已建庭院</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">训练室</th><td data-label="财富">$10,000,000</td><td data-label="每类制作资源">500 普通 + 200 稀有 + 75 史诗</td><td data-label="声誉">9</td><td data-label="其他条件">—</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">牢房走廊及 1 号牢房</th><td data-label="财富">$1,000,000</td><td data-label="每类制作资源">35 稀有</td><td data-label="声誉">8</td><td data-label="其他条件">Raven 在职；有付费内容权限</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">2 号牢房</th><td data-label="财富">$1,500,000</td><td data-label="每类制作资源">50 稀有</td><td data-label="声誉">—</td><td data-label="其他条件">已建走廊；有付费内容权限</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">3 号牢房</th><td data-label="财富">$2,000,000</td><td data-label="每类制作资源">25 史诗</td><td data-label="声誉">—</td><td data-label="其他条件">已建 2 号；有付费内容权限</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">4 号牢房</th><td data-label="财富">$2,500,000</td><td data-label="每类制作资源">30 史诗</td><td data-label="声誉">—</td><td data-label="其他条件">已建 3 号；有付费内容权限</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">5 号牢房</th><td data-label="财富">$3,000,000</td><td data-label="每类制作资源">35 史诗</td><td data-label="声誉">—</td><td data-label="其他条件">已建 4 号；有付费内容权限</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">6 号牢房</th><td data-label="财富">$3,500,000</td><td data-label="每类制作资源">40 史诗</td><td data-label="声誉">—</td><td data-label="其他条件">已建 5 号；有付费内容权限</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">7 号牢房</th><td data-label="财富">$4,000,000</td><td data-label="每类制作资源">45 史诗</td><td data-label="声誉">—</td><td data-label="其他条件">已建 6 号；有付费内容权限</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>大部分委托耗时 <strong>3 小时</strong>，珍兽苑为 <strong>3 小时 20 分钟</strong>，训练室为 <strong>4 小时</strong>。从牢房走廊一直建到 7 号牢房，合计需要 <strong>$17,500,000</strong>。目前没有可委托的 8 号牢房。</p>
<p>庭院连接室外设施；水池是 Sashimi 搬入的条件之一；珍兽苑是带有魔法结界的生物栖息地。庭院、水池、珍兽苑和训练室各提高 1 级装潢。牢房走廊附带 1 号牢房，开放地牢的牢房区域；之后的牢房按顺序扩充收容空间。</p>
</section>
<section id="zh-training"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="zh-Training_Room_apprentices"></span>
<h2>训练室怎么用</h2>
<p>训练室可提升力量、耐力、能力或神秘。每次训练基础消耗为 <strong>$80,000、50 精力和 50 镇定</strong>，没有普通的每日次数上限。安排学徒后，训练时间与加点范围会改善；各结果并非等概率。</p>
<table><thead><tr><th scope="col">学徒数</th><th scope="col">时间</th><th scope="col">属性提升</th><th scope="col">从最低到最高的概率</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">0</th><td data-label="时间">120 分钟</td><td data-label="属性提升">+2 至 +5</td><td data-label="从最低到最高的概率">25%、40%、25%、10%</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">1</th><td data-label="时间">120 分钟</td><td data-label="属性提升">+2 至 +6</td><td data-label="从最低到最高的概率">10%、25%、35%、20%、10%</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">2</th><td data-label="时间">100 分钟</td><td data-label="属性提升">+2 至 +6</td><td data-label="从最低到最高的概率">10%、25%、35%、20%、10%</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">3</th><td data-label="时间">100 分钟</td><td data-label="属性提升">+3 至 +7</td><td data-label="从最低到最高的概率">10%、25%、35%、20%、10%</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>这些行动训练的是玩家自身属性，与员工训练不同。其他适用的行动修正仍可能改变最终显示的费用。</p>
</section>
<section id="zh-rewards">
<h2>交谈、一次性奖励与矿石委托</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th scope="col">行动</th><th scope="col">条件</th><th scope="col">时间与效果</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">和 Gastoff 交谈</th><td data-label="条件">每天最多 6 次</td><td data-label="时间与效果">10 分钟；基础关系 +1，之后再计算修正</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">锻炉哲学</th><td data-label="条件">关系达到「已知」；沟通至少 48</td><td data-label="时间与效果">30 分钟；一次性力量 +1、关系 +10</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">肌肉技艺交流</th><td data-label="条件">关系达到「已遇见」；健美者专长</td><td data-label="时间与效果">40 分钟；一次性吸引力 +1、关系 +5</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">欣赏护甲</th><td data-label="条件">营业时间内</td><td data-label="时间与效果">5 分钟；镇定 +1</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>完成建筑也能提高关系：庭院使 Gastoff 关系 +10，水池 +15，珍兽苑使 Gastoff 与 Aziza 各 +15，训练室使 Gastoff +20，牢房走廊和每间新增牢房各使 Gastoff +10。</p>
<p>战士公会的<strong>铁矿样本</strong>任务要求从 6–10 层收集 5 份样本，奖励 $150、2 声望和 1 水晶；<strong>秘银矿样本</strong>要求从 16–20 层收集 5 份，奖励 $250、3 声望和 1 水晶。任务在公会接取并交付。相关任务进行时，每次生成符合层数的地图都会进行一次 50% 矿石生成判定。拾取矿石不会额外触发战斗，任务样本也不是锻造用矿锭。</p>
</section>
<section id="zh-troubleshooting">
<h2>找不到选项时检查什么</h2>
<ul><li><strong>剑或护甲升级：</strong>检查准确的基础等级与营业时间。Gastoff 的常规升级只到 5 级。</li><li><strong>锻造按钮：</strong>检查是否已有前一级护具，以及完整资源是否足够。时源矿升级还要求完成 Cid 的介绍并持有宝石护具。</li><li><strong>牛头人铁匠：</strong>准备足够支付当前升级的龙币。想再买一次，先离开他的格子，再走回来。</li><li><strong>建筑委托：</strong>检查声誉、前置建筑、所需付费内容权限，以及牢房走廊要求的 Raven 在职状态。已完成的项目会从委托列表消失。</li></ul>
</section>
<section id="zh-related"><h2>相关指南</h2><p>准备锻造资源时可查阅<a href="game-systems-mining-system.html">采矿系统</a>，了解减伤计算可查阅<a href="game-systems-combat-system.html">战斗系统</a>，寻找怪物掉落物则参阅<a href="game-systems-infinity-dungeons.html">无限地下城</a>。进一步升级装备请看<a href="game-systems-sylwithes-hollow.html">Sylwithe 的幽谷</a>，设施经营请看<a href="game-systems-brothel.html">青楼经营</a>。</p></section>
